==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l/en|guess-work}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|guess|work|lang=en}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|giswerk||guesswork}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[estimate]], [[judgment]] or [[opinion]] made by [[guess]]ing, from [[limited]] [[information]].
#* {{quote-book|passage=By a careful study of the figure we might suspect that when the rectangle becomes a square its area would be the greatest, but this would at best be mere '''guesswork'''. A better way would evidently be to plot the graph of the function (1) and note its behavior.|title=[[S:Elements of the Differential and Integral Calculus/Chapter VIII|Elements of the Differential and Integral Calculus]]|author=William Anthony Granville|year=1911}}

